.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_ONE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_one \- look up a single-valued query parameter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_req_query_one(chttpsvr_req *req,
                                      const char *key,
                                      const char **val_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Looks up a query parameter that is expected to appear exactly once.
Unlike chttpsvr_req_query, this function distinguishes an OOM failure
from a missing key and avoids allocating a scratch result array.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success; exactly one value found; stored in *val_out.
ccol_key_not_found; key is absent.
ccol_not_permitted; key appears more than once.
ccol_not_enough_memory; query-string parse buffer could not be allocated.
ccol_invalid_args; req or key is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_oom (3)
